  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "value": "Ubiquitous, with highest expression in heart, kidney, liver and skeletal muscle"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"
      }
     ],
     "value": "The twin CX3C motif contains 4 conserved Cys residues that form 2 disulfide bonds in the mitochondrial intermembrane space. However, during the transit of TIMM13 from cytoplasm into mitochondrion, the Cys residues probably coordinate zinc, thereby preventing folding and allowing its transfer across mitochondrial outer membrane (By similarity)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "DOMAIN"
